 "_about": "Copied from HusbandOutWorld's content/i18n/pt/glossary.json, so the campaign, the novel and the game spell every name the same way. When a spelling changes, change it there and copy it here (or the other way round). \"campaign\" adds this campaign's own names and game words; \"dnd5e\" lists the D&D 5e rules terms of this language's published edition, so players recognise them from their books. Add a new name the first time you translate it.",
 "rule": "Story names stay exactly as in English. That includes coined world terms written as names: creatures, plants, items, nari gels, factions, guilds, places, ranks and coins (Wood People, Sand Worms, Fost Stone, Nari Refresher, Red Winga, Sapphire, Pearl). Plain words around them are translated (nari gel stays, 'soul energy' becomes 'energia da alma'). Exception: the currency balls is written bolas (singular bola), which keeps the double meaning; the rank stays after it (bolas sapphire, bola pearl). Faction names like Beer Balls stay as they are.",
